# Lead-lens sign-off — fix/484-install-banner-brass-and-grid
- date: 2026-11-08
- lead: massimo-vignelli
- supporting: [jony-ive, edward-tufte, dieter-rams, ellen-lupton]

## Findings raised in review, and disposition

F1 AMBER — supportsColour treats FORCE_COLOR="" as unset.
  chalk reads an empty FORCE_COLOR as true. I read it as "not set".
  Kept deliberately: an empty env var is almost always an unset var that
  got exported anyway, and the safe reading of ambiguity here is "no
  colour". Pinned by test so the choice is visible rather than accidental.
  CLEARED — documented in the function body, asserted in the suite.

F2 AMBER — renderBrandMark uses the bare NAME, not renderChip's payload,
  when colour is off. That diverges from the module docstring's claim
  that the chip's payload is identical either way.
  The docstring is about renderChip, which is unchanged and still holds.
  renderBrandMark picks a different cell for a stated reason: with no
  brass plate, the chip's own padding pushes the word one column off the
  grid the art sits on, and buys nothing.
  CLEARED — reason is in the code at the branch.

F3 GREEN — state/luminary-implementations/jony-ive.json carries a
  last_scanned timestamp bump only. Auto-generated, one line, benign.
  CLEARED — no action.

F4 GREEN — the three existing assertions that constrain this change were
  read before editing: the per-line width budget, the indexOf(ART[1])
  check in the CLI test, and the narrow fallback. All survive because
  they use substring checks, and because colour defaults off.
  CLEARED — verified by running the suite, 573 green.

## Lead verdict
Vignelli's own test is whether the system says one thing once. It does:
one brass index, one indent unit, one constant shared by both call sites.
The figlet and the chip both carry the name, which is the system saying
it twice — accepted, and the reason is recorded on the ticket: the chip
has to be the name to work as the recurring mark on later lines, and
install is where a reader first meets it.

No red findings. No amber findings outstanding. Clear to merge.
